---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Closing from '@/components/sections/Closing.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
---

<Base
  title="About Víctor Andújar and Real product"
  description="Meet the product engineer behind Real product. Human judgement for founders who built with AI and are preparing for real users."
  ><section class="wrap page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The human behind the check</p><h1>
      More people can build.<br />That's a good thing.
    </h1>
  </section><section class="wrap section split border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">{site.founder.name}</p><h2>
        Product thinking.<br />Engineering judgement.
      </h2><p class="lead muted mt-8">{site.founder.role}</p>
    </div><div class="prose">
      <p>
        I build digital products, from the experience people see to the systems
        that make it work.
      </p><p>
        AI has opened that process to far more people. Founders can explore an
        idea, build something useful and learn from it without assembling a
        whole team first.
      </p><p>
        I want more of those products to make it into people's hands.
      </p><h2>You keep the wheel.</h2><p>
        Real product exists for the stage after the first working version. When
        you need to know whether a stranger can use it, whether access rules
        hold up and whether the important flows recover when something goes
        wrong.
      </p><p>
        My job is to look carefully, explain what I find and help you decide
        what to do next. Sometimes that means fixing something. Sometimes it
        means leaving it alone.
      </p><h2>What you can expect</h2><ul>
        <li>Evidence you can inspect.</li><li>
          Clear language and honest limits.
        </li><li>Priorities that match your next step.</li><li>
          A product that stays yours.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section><Closing /></Base
>
